320 0 obj
<</E(Accelerating deployment amid manufacturing overcapacity)/K[ 9]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H2/T(Accelerating deployment amid manufacturing overcapacity)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<</E(Global PV is expected to continue rapid growth despite current manufacturing overcapacity \(1 405 GW/year capacity vs. 726 GW production\). Market consolidation likely as module prices stabilize and weaker manufacturers exit. China's market controls may slow capacity additions while diversification to India, USA, EU advances.)/K[ 10]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<</E(Grid integration and storage become critical)/K[ 11]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H2/T(Grid integration and storage become critical)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<</E(As PV penetration exceeds 10% globally and reaches 20-30% in leading markets, curtailment and negative pricing will intensify. Grid reinforcement, storage deployment \(China added 37 GW in 2024\), and demand-side flexibility are urgent priorities. Co-located solar+storage becoming standard in some countries. )/K[ 12 13]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<</E(Diversification into dual-use applications)/K[ 14]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H2/T(Diversification into dual-use applications)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<</E(Agrivoltaics, floating PV \(8.7 GW globally\), BIPV, and infrastructure-integrated systems will gain market share as land-use conflicts intensify. The EU's 403 GW potential for roadside/railway PV and mandatory building solar policies \(EU Solar Strategy, California, Tokyo\) will drive innovation in specialized segments. )/K[ 15]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<</E(Sector coupling unlocks new markets)/K[ 16]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H2/T(Sector coupling unlocks new markets)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<</E(Green hydrogen production \(60 countries with strategies\), EV charging integration \(22% of car sales now electric\), and electrified heating/cooling will create demand beyond traditional electricity markets. Major projects in MENA, Australia advancing with multi-GW solar-to-hydrogen facilities targeting industrial decarbonization.)/K[ 17]/P 51 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
